#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:1
msgid "Integrating with `mise`"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:3
msgid ""
"[`mise`](https://mise.jdx.dev/) is a tool for installing development tools, "
"managing the environment, and running tasks."
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:6
msgid ""
"`just` and `mise` work well together, with `just` defining and running tasks "
"and `mise` installing and managing development tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:9
msgid "To load the `mise` environment within `just`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:20
msgid ""
"The environment is loaded once, when `just` starts, and is available in all "
"recipes. `set dotenv-override` is required, since `mise env` returns a value "
"for the `PATH` variable, which is always already set."
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:24
msgid ""
"`mise` will interactively prompt and ask if `mise.toml` should be trusted. "
"In non-interactive environments, `mise trust` should be run first."
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:27
msgid ""
"`mise env` does not install missing tools, so run `mise install` first, or "
"install missing tools automatically with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:34
msgid "Tool versions can be overridden for the entire justfile:"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:40
msgid "Or for individual recipes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:52
msgid ""
"Alternatively, `set shell` can be used to run every line of every shell "
"recipe with `mise exec`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:62
msgid ""
"And the `[env]` attribute can be used to override tool versions on a per-"
"recipe basis:"
msgstr ""

#: src/integrating-with-mise.md:73
msgid ""
"Note that `mise exec` takes longer to run than `sh`, so `set shell` may make "
"shell recipes with many commands noticeably slower."
msgstr ""
